        ":question/problem": "![](images/6e/6e33e6ee3afde329a12ea5aece03a2bb3e69c3ce34119c668eee98f1d65068c4.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Q$ lies on the segment $MF$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{MO}=n$ and $\\overrightarrow{FO}=d$. The lengths satisfy $MQ:QF=1:1$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OQ}$ in terms of $n$ and $d$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OQ}=$ {{field-1}} $n+$ {{field-2}} $d$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OM}=-n\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OF}=-d .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $M$ through $O$ to $F$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{MF}=\\overrightarrow{MO}+\\overrightarrow{OF}=n-d.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $MQ:QF=1:1$ gives $2$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{MQ}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{MF}=\\frac{1}{2}(n-d).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to M\\to Q$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OQ}&=\\overrightarrow{OM}+\\overrightarrow{MQ}\\\\&=-n+\\frac{1}{2}(n-d)\\\\&=-\\frac{1}{2}n-\\frac{1}{2}d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
