        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OP}=-w\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OT}=n .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $P$ through $O$ to $T$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\overrightarrow{PO}+\\overrightarrow{OT}=w+n.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $PQ:QT=1:1$ gives $2$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\frac{1}{2}(w+n).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to P\\to Q$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OQ}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PQ}\\\\&=-w+\\frac{1}{2}(w+n)\\\\&=-\\frac{1}{2}w+\\frac{1}{2}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested vector has the reverse direction, so negate both coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{QO}=-\\overrightarrow{OQ}=\\frac{1}{2}w-\\frac{1}{2}n.\n$$",
