        ":question/problem": "![](images/05/05562e846465c0cc57e49f48d71247050f8c495aaaff083e5c30af1633fbcf65.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $J$ lies on the segment $DA$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{DO}=t$ and $\\overrightarrow{AO}=v$. The lengths satisfy $DJ:JA=1:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{JO}$ in terms of $t$ and $v$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{JO}=$ {{field-1}} $t+$ {{field-2}} $v$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OD}=-t\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OA}=-v .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $D$ through $O$ to $A$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{DA}=\\overrightarrow{DO}+\\overrightarrow{OA}=t-v.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $DJ:JA=1:5$ gives $6$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{DJ}=\\frac{1}{6}\\overrightarrow{DA}=\\frac{1}{6}(t-v).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to D\\to J$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OJ}&=\\overrightarrow{OD}+\\overrightarrow{DJ}\\\\&=-t+\\frac{1}{6}(t-v)\\\\&=-\\frac{5}{6}t-\\frac{1}{6}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested vector has the reverse direction, so negate both coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{JO}=-\\overrightarrow{OJ}=\\frac{5}{6}t+\\frac{1}{6}v.\n$$",
