        ":question/problem": "![](images/a3/a3091cc929b39094e89086526c005da670621135ac7d76e5e09ab63576569c1a.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $E$ lies on the segment $ZB$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{ZO}=n$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=d$. The lengths satisfy $ZE:EB=1:2$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{EO}$ in terms of $n$ and $d$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{EO}=$ {{field-1}} $n+$ {{field-2}} $d$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OZ}=-n\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OB}=d .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $Z$ through $O$ to $B$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{ZB}=\\overrightarrow{ZO}+\\overrightarrow{OB}=n+d.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $ZE:EB=1:2$ gives $3$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{ZE}=\\frac{1}{3}\\overrightarrow{ZB}=\\frac{1}{3}(n+d).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to Z\\to E$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OE}&=\\overrightarrow{OZ}+\\overrightarrow{ZE}\\\\&=-n+\\frac{1}{3}(n+d)\\\\&=-\\frac{2}{3}n+\\frac{1}{3}d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe requested vector has the reverse direction, so negate both coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{EO}=-\\overrightarrow{OE}=\\frac{2}{3}n-\\frac{1}{3}d.\n$$",
